    "---\n",
    "## Part 6. How long do bad-weather spells last?  (3 pts)\n",
    "*Reference: Week 10 Part B Step 8; Part A §A5 and §A6.*\n",
    "\n",
    "In the Heartland case we could not estimate a transition matrix, because each Ames row was a single sale with no history. Here we **have** the panel data: the same weather system observed day after day. So we can use the counting estimator\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\hat{p}_{ij} = \\frac{\\#\\{\\text{days in state } i \\text{ followed by a day in state } j\\}}{\\#\\{\\text{days in state } i \\text{ with a next day}\\}}$$"
   ]
