    "Our analysis of 365 days (February 2011–January 2012) supports using a simple weather-based staffing model. Holding humidity, wind, and workday status constant, an extra degree Celsius is associated with approximately 114 additional rides. Since apparent temperature nearly duplicates air temperature, adding both creates less stable coefficients with almost no improvement in overall fit. Use the simpler model as a staffing baseline, adjusted to current forecasts.\n",
